        "title": "Apply the law of logarithms to the left hand side (LHS)",
        "text": "Apply the law of logarithms for powers: $$c\\log_b(a)=\\log_b(a**c).$$ \\n $$\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2(x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2(x-3)=\\log_2\\left(x**{1/2}\\right)+\\log_2\\left((x-3)**{1/2}\\right)$$",
        "variabilization": {},
