        ],
        "title": "Apply the law of logarithms to the left hand side (LHS)",
        "text": "Apply the law of logarithms for products: $$\\log_b(a)+\\log_b(c)=\\log_b(ac).$$ \\n $$\\log_2\\left(x**{1/2}\\right)+\\log_2\\left((x-3)**{1/2}\\right)=\\log_2\\left(x**{1/2}(x-3)**{1/2}\\right)$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
